{
  "id": "ebbinghaus-illusion",
  "term": "Ebbinghaus illusion",
  "definition": "The Ebbinghaus illusion is a visual size illusion in which the surrounding context changes how large a central object appears. In this effect, a central circle can seem to change size in the opposite direction to changes in nearby surrounding circles, showing that perceived size is influenced by contextual visual cues.",
